"10"},{"s":"congrats"}]},"codeShots":true,"why":"A photoelectric smoke alarm, its cover off, high on the living-room wall: a light beam crosses a dark chamber, smoke from a burning trash can drifts up, a side sensor catches the light the smoke bounces, a horn makes it loud, and a counter shows it lasts 10 years. The camera opens close on the dark chamber and its beam, frames the alarm with the smoke rising, and ends on the room.","hold":true},"sentences":[{"role":"hook","text":"If you shine a light beam through a dark box, you have a smoke detector."},{"role":"problem","text":"But when smoke drifts up from a burning trash can, the beam just keeps shining."},{"role":"fix1","text":"So you add a sensor off to the side, and smoke bounces light onto it."},{"role":"problem2","text":"But a sensor makes no sound, and at night everyone sleeps through the fire."},{"role":"fix2","text":"So you add a horn that blares at least 85 decibels at 10 feet."},{"role":"name","text":"This is a photoelectric smoke detector."},{"role":"fact","text":"Fire safety experts say to replace it every 10 years."},{"role":"finish","text":"Add a battery, a test button and vents."},{"role":"congrats","text":"Congratulations, you have built a smoke detector."}]}